done-so-far: found by making the mistake myself. Reading per-run.csv by the `pass` column alone I
  reported the resident model at 73/88 with `fix` 10/18; the truth is 51/52. Fourteen of the
  fifteen "failures" were an agent process dying (rc=1), the gateway crashing (rc=2) or a timeout,
  on a model build DELETED on 2026-07-13. `summarize_matrix.py` declares NON_CAPABILITY_RC={1,2}
  and its own docstring promises those are "EXCLUDED from every rate" — but `rate()` is
  sum(pass)/len(rows), so an infra failure inside a healthy model still counts against it.
next: apply the constant the file already declares, print what was excluded so it can be neither
  lost nor counted, mirror it in the byte-identical .ssc twin, and cover it with a test.
